---
// Stylized representation of a Bookwise note — quote block with thinking
// layer beneath. Uses the app's actual color tokens and serif face.
---
<div class="bg-white rounded-hero shadow-strong border border-line p-6 md:p-8 max-w-md mx-auto">
  <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-5">
    <span class="text-[10px] font-sans font-bold tracking-[0.15em] uppercase text-accent-deep bg-accent-pale px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full">
      Quote
    </span>
    <span class="text-[10px] font-sans font-bold tracking-[0.15em] uppercase text-ink-muted">
      p. 142
    </span>
  </div>

  <blockquote class="font-serif italic text-xl md:text-2xl text-ink leading-snug border-l-2 border-accent pl-4">
    "We are what we pretend to be, so we must be careful about what we pretend to be."
  </blockquote>
  <p class="font-sans text-xs text-ink-muted mt-2 pl-4">— Mother Night, Kurt Vonnegut</p>

  <div class="mt-6 pt-5 border-t border-line">
    <p class="text-[10px] font-sans font-bold tracking-[0.15em] uppercase text-ink-muted mb-2">
      Thinking
    </p>
    <p class="font-serif text-base text-ink leading-relaxed">
      The whole novel pivots on this. <span class="bg-accent-pale px-1 rounded-sm">Pretending</span> isn't separate from being — it shapes it. Reminds me of <span class="text-accent-deep font-semibold">[[Sartre on bad faith]]</span>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-1.5 mt-5">
    <span class="text-[10px] font-sans font-semibold tracking-wider uppercase text-ink-muted bg-paper px-2 py-1 rounded-full border border-line">
      IDENTITY
    </span>
    <span class="text-[10px] font-sans font-semibold tracking-wider uppercase text-ink-muted bg-paper px-2 py-1 rounded-full border border-line">
      FICTION
    </span>
  </div>
</div>
